{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>A sound of tumult from the city.</b> Zion." "<b>A sound from the temple.</b> HaShem — it is the house of HaShem, or the heavens, for they are called the holy temple. And the sense is a sound that will be heard in all the world: the vengeance of HaShem upon them." "<b>His enemies.</b> They are the excommunicators."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:09.948301955Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}